From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 20:05:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: lpass-msm8998: add missing const on variant
 pointers

struct lpass_data.variant is const (sound/soc/qcom/lpass.h), and every
other lpass-*.c CPU DAI driver in the tree (lpass-cpu.c, lpass-sc7180.c,
lpass-sc7280.c) declares its local copy as
`const struct lpass_variant *`. lpass-msm8998.c was the one outlier,
dropping the qualifier in msm8998_lpass_alloc_dma_channel() and
msm8998_lpass_init(). Harmless under GCC, but fatal under this tree's
Clang/LLVM build (-Werror,-Wincompatible-pointer-types-discards-qualifiers).

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/lpass-msm8998.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/lpass-msm8998.c b/sound/soc/qcom/lpass-msm8998.c
index b8f063406925..0830a641b0d9 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/lpass-msm8998.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/lpass-msm8998.c
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ static struct snd_soc_dai_driver msm8998_lpass_cpu_dai_driver[] = {
 static int msm8998_lpass_alloc_dma_channel(struct lpass_data *drvdata,
 					   int direction, unsigned int dai_id)
 {
-	struct lpass_variant *v = drvdata->variant;
+	const struct lpass_variant *v = drvdata->variant;
 	int chan = 0;
 
 	if (dai_id == LPASS_DP_RX) {
@@ -149,7 +149,7 @@ static int msm8998_lpass_free_dma_channel(struct lpass_data *drvdata, int chan,
 static int msm8998_lpass_init(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct lpass_data *drvdata = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
-	struct lpass_variant *variant = drvdata->variant;
+	const struct lpass_variant *variant = drvdata->variant;
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	int ret, i;
 
